<title>POLAND: Poland sells PLN 150 mln one-year bonds.</title>
<headline>Poland sells PLN 150 mln one-year bonds.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland sold 150 million zlotys of one-year index-linked bonds, the amount on offer, after investors bid for 352 million zlotys worth of the bonds, the finance ministry said.</p>
<p>The minimum accepted price rose to 96.67 from 95.00 at the last auction of the bonds on October 29.</p>
<p>Average price was also up to 96.74 from 95.99.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 2 653 9700</p>
</text>
